_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039287/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-104780" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The notation $f:X\\to Y$ means that the function $f$ maps the set $X$ to the set $Y.$ In this case,\n\n- the domain of $f$ is $X,$\n\n- the codomain of $f$ is $Y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our functions.\n\n- The domain of $p$ is $Z,$ the set of integers.\n\n- The domain of $q$ is $(0,7),$ the interval from $0$ to $7$ (excluding $0$ and $7$).\n\n- The domain of $r$ is ${Z}^{+},$ the set of positive integers.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039287/state.json" "file_sha256" "8ecff6f2c2567a11634c4a5cc42a2123fdd92c0cd321ab4ef663777f3db75093" "basis" 1355 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039287/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-104780" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039287/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f655e9e4af250bb6f9f43018e3cfe012e6a10dbafb1483ab3ba97af93a8ddc5f" "basis" 1355 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039287/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-104780" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039287/state.json" "file_sha256" "8ecff6f2c2567a11634c4a5cc42a2123fdd92c0cd321ab4ef663777f3db75093" "basis" 1355 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039287/ed