uestion" "q-96820" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{x}^{2}={x}^{3}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039287/state.json" "file_sha256" "8ecff6f2c2567a11634c4a5cc42a2123fdd92c0cd321ab4ef663777f3db75093" "basis" 1355 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039287/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-96820" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "h(x)={x}^{2}-{x}^{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039287/state.json" "file_sha256" "8ecff6f2c2567a11634c4a5cc42a2123fdd92c0cd321ab4ef663777f3db75093" "basis" 1355 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039287/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-96830" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039287/assets/740d578e554cd61bc733079c32c063d41ab4d9dcc775d36f7080ee8e5aa5a622.png)\n\nConsider the function $f:X\\to Y$ given by the mapping diagram shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The domain of $f$ is ${5,10,15}$\n- The codomain of $f$ is ${5,10,12,13,14,15}$\n- The range of $f$ is ${12,13,14}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039287/state.json" "file_sha256" "8ecff6f2c2567a11634c4a5cc42a2123fdd92c0cd321ab4ef663777f3db75093" "basis" 1355 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039287/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-96830" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The notation $f:X\\to Y$ means that the function $f$ maps the set $X$ to the set $Y.$ In this case,\n\n- the domain of $f$ is $X,$\n\n- the codomain of $f$ is $Y.$\n\nThe range of $f$ is the subset of the codomain that contains all values $y\\in Y$ that are mapped to by at least one element $x\\in X.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect our diagram:\n\n- the domain of $f$ is $X={5,10,15},$\n\n- the codomain of $f$ is $Y={12,13,14},$\n\n- the range of $f$ is ${12,13},$ the subset of elements of $Y$ that have at least one incoming arrow.\n\nAs a result, statements II and III are false, while statement I is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer \"I only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039287/state.json" "file_sha256" "8ecff6f2c2567a11634c4a5cc42a2123fdd92c0cd321ab4ef663777f3db75093" "basis" 1355 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039287/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-96830" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039287/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f655e9e4af250bb6f9f43018e3cfe012e6a10dbafb1483ab3ba97af93a8ddc5f" "basis" 1355 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039287/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-96830" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039287/state.json" "file_sha256" "8ecff6f2c2567a11634c4a5cc42a2123fdd92c0cd321ab4ef663777f3db75093" "basis" 1355 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039287/edb-import/verifica