ute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "f:x↦x+{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072015/state.json" "file_sha256" "5d703f10ddc0645c44cdf6e02c347df5b72ddf9c1cf4cdaf7ff503aaf578ab29"} {"question" "q-96123" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072015/assets/dcee145044fe79dc7f4d07c3c4c1248df358cd8eda7a173cd8d4641f13404122.png)\n\nConsider the function $f:X\\to Y$ given by the mapping diagram shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The domain of $f$ is ${0,1,2,3}$\n- The codomain of $f$ is ${0,-1}$\n- The range of $f$ is ${0,-1}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072015/state.json" "file_sha256" "5d703f10ddc0645c44cdf6e02c347df5b72ddf9c1cf4cdaf7ff503aaf578ab29"} {"question" "q-96123" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The notation $f:X\\to Y$ means that the function $f$ maps the set $X$ to the set $Y.$ In this case,\n\n- the domain of $f$ is $X,$\n\n- the codomain of $f$ is $Y.$\n\nThe range of $f$ is the subset of the codomain that contains all values $y\\in Y$ that are mapped to by at least one element $x\\in X.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect our diagram:\n\n- the domain of $f$ is $X={0,1,2,3},$\n\n- the codomain of $f$ is $Y={0,-1,-2},$\n\n- the range of $f$ is ${0,-1},$ the subset of elements of $Y$ that have at least one incoming arrow.\n\nAs a result, statements I and III are true, while statement II is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer \"I and III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072015/state.json" "file_sha256" "5d703f10ddc0645c44cdf6e02c347df5b72ddf9c1cf4cdaf7ff503aaf578ab29"} {"question" "q-96123" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072015/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3259e187ee32b0bee483a5f56570bfbf6a0ed0503edeef142bd2fc5b7db4cba8"} {"question" "q-96123" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072015/state.json" "file_sha256" "5d703f10ddc0645c44cdf6e02c347df5b72ddf9c1cf4cdaf7ff503aaf578ab29"} {"question" "q-96123" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "I, II, and III"] ["text" "II and III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072015/state.json" "file_sha256" "5d703f10ddc0645c44cdf6e02c347df5b72ddf9c1cf4cdaf7ff503aaf578ab29"} {"question" "q-96123" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072015/state.json" "file_sha256" "5d703f10ddc0645c44cdf6e02c347df5b72ddf9c1cf4cdaf7ff503aaf578ab29"} {"question" "q-104946" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following is the correct interpretation of $g:Q\\to R?$\n\n- The domain of $g$ is $R$\n- The codomain of $g$ is $R$\n- The range of $g$ is $Q$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072015/state.json" "file_sha256" "5d703f10ddc0645c44cdf6e02c347df5b72ddf9c1cf4cdaf7ff503aaf578ab29"} {"question" "q-104946" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The notation \n\n$$\ng:Q\\to R\n$$\n\nmeans that the function $g$ maps the set $Q$ to the set $R.$ In this case,\n\n- the domain of $g$ is $Q,$ and\n\n- the codomain of $g$ is $R.$ Note that $Q⊂R$ is *not* necessarily the range.\n\nAs a result, statements I and III are false, while statement II is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072015/state.json" "file_sha256" "5d703f10ddc0645c44cdf6e02c347df5b72ddf9c1cf4cdaf7ff503aaf578ab29"} {"question" "q-104946" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072015/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3259e187ee32b0bee483a5f56570bfbf6a0ed0503edeef142bd2fc5b7db4cba8"} {"question" "q-104946" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072015/state.json" "file_sha256" "5d703f10ddc0645c44cdf6e02c347df5b72ddf9c1cf4cdaf7ff503aaf578ab29"} {"question" "q-104946" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072015/state.json" "file_sha256" "5d703f10ddc0645c44cdf6e02c347df5b72ddf9c1cf4cdaf7ff503aaf578ab29"} {"question" "q-104946" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072015/state.json" "file_sha256" "5d703f10ddc0645c44cdf6e02c347df5b72ddf9c1cf4cdaf7ff503aaf578ab29"} {"question" "q-96830" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072015/assets/740d578e554cd61bc733079c32c063d41ab4d9dcc775d36f7080ee8e5aa5a622.png)\n\nConsider the function $f:X\\to Y$ given by the mapping diagram shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The domain of $f$ is ${5,10,15}$\n- The codomain of $f$ is ${5,10,12,13,14,15}$\n- The range of $f$ is ${12,13,14}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072015/state.json" "file_sha256" "5d703f10ddc0645c44cdf6e02c347df5b72ddf9c1cf4cdaf7ff503aaf578ab29"} {"question" "q-96830" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The notation $f:X\\to Y$ means that the function $f$ maps the set $X$ to the set $Y.$ In this case,\n\n- the domain of $f$ is $X,$\n\n- the codomain of $f$ is $Y.$\n\nThe range of $f$ is the subset of the codomain that contains all values $y\\in Y$ that are mapped to by at least one element $x\\in X.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect our diagram:\n\n- the domain of $f$ is $X={5,10,15},$\n\n- the codomain of $f$ is $Y={12,13,14},$\n\n- the range of $f$ is ${12,13},$ the subset of elements of $Y$ that have at least one incoming arrow.\n\nAs a result, statements II and III are false, while statement I is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer \"I only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072015/state.json" "file_sha256" "5d703f10ddc0645c44cdf6e02c347df5b72ddf9c1cf4cdaf7ff503aaf578ab29"} {"question" "q-96830" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072015/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3259e187ee32b0bee483a5f56570bfbf6a0ed0503edeef142bd2fc5b7db4cba8"} {"question" "q-96830" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/