 function $f$ maps the set $[-1,1]$ to the set $R.$ In this case,\n\n- the domain of $f$ is $[-1,1],$ and\n\n- the codomain of $f$ is $R.$ Note that this is *not* necessarily the range.\n\nAs a result, statements II and III are false, while statement I is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072015/state.json" "file_sha256" "5d703f10ddc0645c44cdf6e02c347df5b72ddf9c1cf4cdaf7ff503aaf578ab29"} {"question" "q-96825" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072015/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3259e187ee32b0bee483a5f56570bfbf6a0ed0503edeef142bd2fc5b7db4cba8"} {"question" "q-96825" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072015/state.json" "file_sha256" "5d703f10ddc0645c44cdf6e02c347df5b72ddf9c1cf4cdaf7ff503aaf578ab29"} {"question" "q-96825" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072015/state.json" "file_sha256" "5d703f10ddc0645c44cdf6e02c347df5b72ddf9c1cf4cdaf7ff503aaf578ab29"} {"question" "q-96825" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072015/state.json" "file_sha256" "5d703f10ddc0645c44cdf6e02c347df5b72ddf9c1cf4cdaf7ff503aaf578ab29"} {"question" "e-8474" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following functions has the codomain $[0,1]?$\n\n- $p: \\{ 0, 1 \\} \\to \\mathbb{R}$\n\n- $q: \\mathbb{R} \\to [ 0, 1 ]$\n\n- $r: [0,1] \\to [ 0, 1 )$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072015/example-8474.json" "file_sha256" "4547218e3d329e5548e8110e1227f9c5d03f72cb152f484296c92925037af105"} {"question" "e-8474" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The notation $f: X \\to Y$ means that the function $f$ maps the set $X$ to the set $Y.$ In this case,\n\n- the domain of $f$ is $X,$\n\n- the codomain of $f$ is $Y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our functions.\n\n- The codomain of $p$ is $\\mathbb{R},$ the set of real numbers.\n\n- The codomain of $q$ is $[ 0, 1 ],$ the interval from $0$ and $1$ (including $0$ and $1$).\n\n- The codomain of $r$ is $[ 0, 1),$ the interval from $0$ to $1$ (including $0$ but not including $1$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072015/example-8474.json" "file_sha256" "4547218e3d329e5548e8110e1227f9c5d03f72cb152f484296c92925037af105"} {"question" "e-8475" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following is the correct symbolic notation for the sentence given below?\n\n$\\qquad$ *\"The function $g$ maps the set of rational numbers to the set $Y$.\"*\n\n- $g:\\mathbb{Q} \\to Y$\n\n- $g: Y \\to \\mathbb{Q}$\n\n- $g:\\mathbb{R} \\to Y$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072015/example-8475.json" "file_sha256" "f936f393645382949563b3519f371e887bf7066990a1e1798a2882bf4486cd53"} {"question" "e-8475" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The sentence *\"The function $g$ maps the set of rational numbers to the set $Y$\"* is equivalent to the following symbolic notation:\n\n$\\qquad$ $g:\\mathbb{Q} \\to Y$\n\nHere, the domain of $g$ is $\\mathbb Q,$ and the codomain of $g$ is $Y.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072015/example-8475.json" "file_sha256" "f936f393645382949563b3519f371e887bf7066990a1e1798a2882bf4486cd53"} {"question" "e-8476" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following is equivalent to $g(x)=x-x^3?$\n\n- $g:x \\mapsto x-x^3$\n\n- $g:x \\mapsto -x^3$\n\n- $g:-x \\mapsto x^3$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072015/example-8476.json" "file_sha256" "7dc102c1d4d8202a72e833a78eb2b00bbf65a31607ebdb504be7e0de3873f9d3"} {"question" "e-8476" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The notation $g(x)=x-x^3$ means that the function $g$ maps the element $x$ in the domain to $x-x^3$ in the codomain. This can also be written as\n\n$$\ng:x \\mapsto x-x^3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072015/example-8476.json" "file_sha256" "7dc102c1d4d8202a72e833a78eb2b00bbf65a31607ebdb504be7e0de3873f9d3"} {"question" "e-8487" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following is the correct interpretation of $g: \\{ -1,0,1 \\} \\to \\mathbb{R}?$\n\n- The domain of $g$ is $\\{ -1,0,1 \\}$\n\n- The codomain of $g$ is $\\mathbb{R}$\n\n- The range of $g$ is $\\mathbb{R}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072015/example-8487.json" "file_sha256" "e26d8577f0a564cadc7fdde2d6fdde16be5c6d90eaa6c47172c977f8e4478c62"} {"question" "e-8487" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The notation \n\n$$\ng: \\{ -1,0,1 \\} \\to \\mathbb{R}\n$$\n\nmeans that the function $g$ maps the set $\\{ -1,0,1 \\}$ 